# Copy to .env.production before running `npm run build` for a real
# deployment — Vite loads this automatically for production builds, no
# flag needed. Unlike the backend's env vars, this gets baked into the
# static JS bundle at build time, not read at runtime, so it must be set
# correctly *before* building, and changing it means rebuilding.
#
# With the Caddyfile as shipped (dashboard + API on the same domain),
# this is just that domain — same-origin, so this isn't even a
# cross-origin request from the browser's point of view (CORS_ORIGIN on
# the backend still gets set to match, for the same reason belt-and-braces
# beats relying on same-origin alone).
VITE_API_URL=https://REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_DOMAIN
